# voxely-local-runtime

The daily driver is `src-tauri/target/release/voxely.exe` (optimized Rust/Vite, compile flag `VOXELY_LOCAL_BUILD=1` so the UI still says local). Not `tauri dev`, not `tauri build -d`, and not the installed `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Voxely` copy.

After a wave that changes Rust, frontend, or anything the running app should show:

1. Stop running `voxely.exe` if it locks the binary (`Access is denied` on overwrite means it is still running).
2. Rebuild with `bun run local:release` (or `$env:VOXELY_LOCAL_BUILD='1'; bunx tauri build --no-bundle`).
3. Start `src-tauri/target/release/voxely.exe` again if the script did not.
4. Prove the user is on that build before claiming the wave is done: the running process path is that release exe, `CreationDate`/`StartTime` is at or after the exe `LastWriteTime`, and the expected HWND exists (main and/or overlay, matching the change). Title is `Voxely (local)` / `Voxely (локальная версия)`.

Do not leave the user on a stale exe. Do this on every such wave without waiting to be asked.

If the user says the app is still broken, first re-check the running path and timestamps. Do not debug a different binary than the one on screen.
